  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img height=\"154\" src=\"assets\\st0131_66344498b0ea.png\" width=\"124\" /><br /><br />The hydrogen atoms in <math><mi>O</mi><mi>H</mi></math> bond are ionizable and are acidic whereas the hydrogen atoms in&nbsp;<math><mi>P</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>H</mi></math> bonds have reducing property. There are two such <math><mi>P</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>H</mi></math> bonds in Hypophosphours acid.</p></blockquote>"
